# q2_compare
Task 2.2 / 2.3  allocation policies on the same workload
disk 68 GB, block 4096 B, 6000 + 2000 files, every third file deleted

policy                   | time ms |   extents | failed | largest GB | frag % | 1 GB?
-------------------------+---------+-----------+--------+------------+--------+------
contiguous first fit     |     4.0 |   1897519 |      0 |      13.69 |  10.72 |   yes
contiguous best fit      |     8.1 |   3422730 |      0 |      14.98 |   2.33 |   yes
contiguous worst fit     |    12.6 |   4008000 |     20 |       0.01 |  99.90 |    no
   (20 of the 2000 new files could not be placed)
indexed (one index block) |     2.9 |     17998 |      0 |      15.32 |   0.00 |   yes

extents = free extents examined to place every file;
frag %  = 1 - largest free extent / all free blocks

reads needed to reach the last block of a 4 GB file (4 KB blocks)
  contiguous : 1 read  (one seek to start + length)
  indexed    : 2 reads (the index block, then the data block)
  linked/FAT : 1048576 reads (one per block in the chain)
  walking the chain in RAM took 2.27 ms, i.e. 2.2 ns per hop;
  on a disk each hop is a seek, so the same walk costs seconds.
